  offerDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - For your first job, you will construct a bridge over a 30m <color=#FFB347>span
      using standard road decking and piers.
    - The piers will serve as your deep <color=#FFB347>foundation, transferring the
      downward compression safely into the riverbed.
    - I am giving you a strict <color=#FFB347>budget of 15,000 to procure all necessary
      materials.
    - Before you draft your design at the <color=#FFB347>workbench, I want you to
      go inspect the live <color=#FFB347>load vehicle we will be using to test its
      structural integrity.
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - 'Still here? The wood is ready. The design is simple: Road, and Piers'
    - A beam bridge is the foundation of everything else. Build it, and we can move
      forward
    - Just add the piers below the road
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - It held! My cart crossed without a problem. This crossing is connected again
    - 'See you on the other side of the bridge

'
